# (AI-assisted) 60 fps sweep: every checkpoint in game order in the late-game world (all tasks
# closed, 100 power cells, as playthrough_late.pad), for config.ini fps_cap = 60 and
# stats_period = 5. At each checkpoint: continue, wait until Jak stands (target-stance; the two
# Lava Tube middle checkpoints: target-racing), 3 s more, the marker "fps60 N NAME", then ~15 s
# (900 frames) turning the camera slowly (right stick half left, ~2 turns) while Jak stands.
# get-current-time is logged at the marker and at the end (game time in 1/300 s: with the pad
# frames in between it gives the mean time ratio, i.e. whether game time per frame is right).
# Read: platform/3ds/tools/fps60_report.py gk.log (per checkpoint: fps from the stats windows
# that start after the marker). ~30-45 min (frames, not seconds: slower at lower fps).
# Hardware: copy to sdmc:/3ds/jak1/fps60_sweep.pad, config.ini "pad_script = fps60_sweep.pad"
# (platform/3ds/tests/fps60_hw_config.ini). Format and commands: game/sce/pad_script.h
0 wait *target* target-title-wait
150 tasks 2 111
160 call poke32 $*game-info* 92 f100
200 log CP 1 training-start
200 continue training-start
201 wait *target* target-continue
202 wait *target* target-stance
382 pos *target*
383 call get-current-time
384 log fps60 1 training-start
385 rx=64
